# Applied to submitted mail only (see submission-cleanup in master.cf).
#
# Strips the Received header this server would otherwise add for the
# submitting client, which carries the staff member's home or hotel IP address
# to every recipient. That address is also frequently on a consumer blocklist,
# so removing it is worth a point of reputation as well as the privacy.
#
# Only the ESMTPSA hop is removed. The rest of the chain is evidence and stays.
/^Received:.*with ESMTPSA/     IGNORE
/^X-Originating-IP:/           IGNORE
/^X-Mailer:/                   IGNORE
/^User-Agent:/                 IGNORE
